1
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,080
There. Beautiful.

2
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:03,680
Thank you.

3
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:05,239
Are you two really being lovebirds,

4
00:01:05,319 --> 00:01:07,240
or is this just an act?

5
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,400
We agreed to stay married.

6
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:13,640
Get all those trees out of here.
I don't like them.

7
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,880
Neen, Neen!

8
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:18,160
Please listen to me!

9
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:20,800
Stop bullshitting me! Stop it!

10
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:22,800
- Stop it!
- Neen, that's enough!

11
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,880
Then you can stay with her all you want.

12
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:27,680
No matter how hard it is,

13
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,840
I won't let go of her hand.

14
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,880
You're together almost all the time,

15
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,080
yet she still found a way to surprise you.

16
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:45,440
Ms. Runch is awesome.

17
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,280
She was here?

18
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:50,920
Yes. She just left.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,040
Wait, you didn't see each other?

20
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,320
Runch!

21
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,479
Neen.

22
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,960
I was just stopping by quietly.

23
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,560
You didn't have to come out here.

24
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,520
Take your flowers.

25
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:26,200
You think a bouquet of flowers
can fix everything?

26
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:39,960
Yes, Mom?

27
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,120
I'm not at the office yet.

28
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,120
I'll call you when I get there.

29
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:45,240
Bye.

30
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,440
Second attempt.

31
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:19,960
What can I get you?

32
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,200
I'd like these three, please.

33
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,280
Sure.

34
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,240
Can I earn M points here?

35
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:29,640
Yes. You may scan your receipt
on the M Card app

36
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,520
to earn M points.

37
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,120
- Can I scan to pay?
- Sure.

38
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,160
Dessert, from Ms. Runch.

39
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,840
They're all yours, Ms. Nat.

40
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,520
Flowers, from Ms. Runch.

41
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,960
Please get them out of here.

42
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,880
- Chocolate, from--
- I know.

43
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,640
Please get that out of here.

44
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:05,520
MOM

45
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,480
For this matter,

46
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:19,839
I'd like to change our whole plan.

47
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,320
Please turn over to page…

48
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:28,920
Excuse me, Ms. Runch. Your mother called.

49
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,440
Please excuse me.

50
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:46,040
Yes, Mom? Is something wrong?

51
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,760
<i>Nothing, honey.</i>

52
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,200
<i>I'm perfectly fine.</i>

53
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:51,880
<i>I was just wondering</i>
<i>if you've had lunch yet.</i>

54
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,680
Mom, I'm in a meeting.

55
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:58,040
<i>I'm sorry, honey.</i>

56
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,920
<i>I really didn't know.</i>

57
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,960
MOM

58
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:23,040
Yes, Mom?

59
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,080
<i>Have you left the office yet, Runch?</i>

60
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,640
Not yet, Mom. I'm still finishing my work.

61
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:31,800
Did you eat yet?
Do you want me to bring you food?

62
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:34,360
I'm not hungry yet.

63
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:37,200
Remember to eat. And did you
take the vitamins I sent you?

64
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,600
<i>You need to take them, honey.</i>

65
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,800
Okay, Mom.

66
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,880
I should get back to work now.

67
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:46,560
I care about you, honey.

68
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,160
I know.

69
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,240
Mom.

70
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:53,240
Oh, Runch.

71
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,440
You're home.

72
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:57,440
I fell asleep for a bit.

73
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:58,640
Mom…

74
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,760
Why didn't you go to bed in your room?

75
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:01,920
Why'd you wait for me?

76
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,960
I was worried about you.

77
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:06,960
I called, but you wouldn't answer.

78
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,480
I got anxious, so I sat here and waited

79
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:11,640
so that I'd see you when you got home.

80
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,040
You know,

81
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:16,920
you don't have to call me
all the time, Mom.

82
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,800
I have work to do.

83
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:20,720
Sometimes I really can't
answer your calls.

84
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:24,760
I understand.
I didn't mean to disturb you.

85
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,160
I'm just happy

86
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:28,720
to be alone together with you like this.

87
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,560
Whatever you do,

88
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:35,040
wherever you are, or whether you're tired,
I want to know it all.

89
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,920
And I care about you.

90
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:37,840
Plus,

91
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:40,920
it's been a while since we had
our mother-daughter bonding time.

92
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,920
Since you got married,

93
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:46,080
this is the first time
you've been this close to me.

94
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,880
I didn't mean to stay away from you.

95
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,280
I know.

96
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:57,000
I'm not upset.

97
00:07:58,080 --> 00:08:00,000
I just missed you.

98
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,080
You should go to bed.

99
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:07,960
I know.

100
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,400
So should you, Mom.

101
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:13,280
- Sure.
- Let's both go to bed.

102
00:08:35,799 --> 00:08:36,720
My ring!

103
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,080
Hello, Mom.

104
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,560
Yes, honey?

105
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:56,640
Could you check in the bathroom for me?

106
00:08:56,720 --> 00:09:00,320
I remember taking off my ring
and putting it by the sink.

107
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:02,160
I forgot to wear it today.

108
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:09,240
I checked. I didn't see a ring.

109
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:10,440
You didn't?

110
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,880
Are you sure?

111
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:17,160
I could swear
I put it by the sink, though.

112
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:20,000
I'm very sure. I looked all over.

113
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,720
There was no ring.

114
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,040
How strange.

115
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,840
But I swear I left it by the sink.

116
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,040
<i>Don't worry, honey.</i>

117
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:32,520
Maybe you put it somewhere else.

118
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,200
I'll help you find it.

119
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:37,040
I'll search all over the place again.

120
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:40,680
If I find it,
I'll let you know right away.

121
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,040
Where on earth is it?

122
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,080
It's not here.

123
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:38,320
What? The bag's replaced?

124
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:51,680
Runch.

125
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,080
Runch, where are you going?

126
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:55,120
Runch!

127
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,360
Runch!

128
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:23,280
What are you doing?

129
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:25,200
I'm looking for my ring.

130
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:26,680
I told you,

131
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:28,600
I didn't find a ring in the bathroom.

132
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,200
You don't believe me?

133
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,920
I distinctly remember

134
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,480
putting it by the sink, Mom.

135
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:38,200
Hey, will you stop it!

136
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:40,320
Stop looking already! It's dirty!

137
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,000
It's just a ring. What's the big deal?

138
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,760
It's not just a ring.

139
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:57,880
It's my wedding ring with Neen.

140
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,800
It means a lot to me.

141
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:03,360
I have to find it, no matter what.

142
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:08,400
If it's not here, that means it's gone.

143
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,160
What do you mean by that?

144
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:16,960
What I mean is

145
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:19,000
some things shouldn't be kept

146
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:21,240
if it pains everyone in the house.

147
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,440
Why would you say that?

148
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:25,080
Don't tell me…

149
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:32,280
you threw away my ring.

150
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:37,800
Well, it was right in front of me.

151
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:40,080
And it made me feel uncomfortable.

152
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,160
I'm asking you,

153
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:45,320
you threw away my ring, didn't you?

154
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:54,120
Where did you throw it away to?

155
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:58,280
Uh, Runch--

156
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,360
Answer me!

157
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:00,960
Answer me, Mom!

158
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,840
Runch, that hurts! Let me go, will you?

159
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:06,600
So that ring matters more than me?

160
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:09,640
Where is the ring, Mom?

161
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:18,760
<i>Mothers will do anything,</i>

162
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:22,120
<i>especially one</i>
<i>who's as protective as yours.</i>

163
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:25,360
<i>She'd do it just so she wouldn't</i>
<i>lose you to someone else.</i>

164
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:29,000
<i>I think you fell for your mother's trick.</i>

165
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,560
Mom.

166
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:38,800
Please go home.

167
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:42,080
Are you mad at me?

168
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,040
I'm not.

169
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:48,080
But you're crossing the line.

170
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:51,880
Runch, I'm sorry.

171
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:53,360
I didn't think it through

172
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:55,240
What I did was wrong.

173
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,600
Please don't kick me out.

174
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:58,240
I have no one else to turn to.

175
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,200
I want to stay with you.

176
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:03,840
That's all I ask.

177
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:00,480
Runch! No!

178
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:05,440
It's me, it's me!

179
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:07,920
Why were you following me?

180
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,520
You scared me!

181
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:12,120
My eyes are burning.

182
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:15,400
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to. It's just…

183
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:18,440
I didn't want you to walk away,

184
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:21,120
so I followed you quietly.

185
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:23,600
I didn't think you'd spray me
right in the face.

186
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:30,200
I'm sorry for scaring you.

187
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,640
But actually,

188
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:38,480
I need your help with something.

189
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:40,920
What do you need my help for?

190
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:44,920
I want us to team up

191
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,120
and get my mom to show her true colors.

192
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,000
Am I hearing this right?

193
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,360
Yes.

194
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,240
You heard me right.

195
00:16:58,680 --> 00:16:59,920
But I probably

196
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,440
can't handle this alone.

197
00:17:04,319 --> 00:17:06,480
If you want my mom to go home,

198
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,119
we have to work together.

199
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,200
What are you doing?

200
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,880
Mom, you're back!

201
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:46,800
Did you miss me, Mom?

202
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:48,840
You're speechless.

203
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,520
That means you did miss me.

204
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:53,840
Mom, I'm back.

205
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:55,440
I've come back to stay here,

206
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:57,520
and I'm not going anywhere this time.

207
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:00,440
I'll make sure you see my face every day.

208
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:02,320
- But--
- Let's get along

209
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:05,080
so Runch can rest easy, Mom.

210
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:08,240
From now on, I will listen to you.

211
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:10,880
I'll never ever go against you.

212
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:14,320
I love you, Mom.

213
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,200
I love you so much.

214
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:21,880
Did you miss me, Mom?

215
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:24,640
Gosh, I missed you so bad.

216
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:27,720
I promise I won't leave you again, Mom.

217
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:41,840
That brat!

218
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:44,240
What do I need to do to get rid of you?

219
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:46,200
What should I do now?

220
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:09,080
<i>Would you all like</i>

221
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:11,680
<i>to join us for dinner</i>
<i>at my daughter's tomorrow?</i>

222
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,560
Thank you.

223
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:43,320
I was thinking

224
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:46,160
I'd invite my friends
to join us for dinner here today.

225
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:48,400
Could you take care of it, Neen?

226
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,480
I want a full course meal,

227
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:54,280
and I want you
in charge of the whole meal.

228
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:56,800
This evening?

229
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:00,720
I'm not sure if I can prepare it in time.

230
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:02,600
There's not nearly enough time.

231
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,440
You'll have to figure it out.

232
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:07,080
I already invited them.

233
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:18,720
Neen,

234
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:21,360
please do this for my mom.

235
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:24,360
Don't disappoint her.

236
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:31,200
Okay.

237
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:50,000
Neen,

238
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:52,600
you've been on your phone all day.

239
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:55,360
You didn't get the place ready
or anything.

240
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,240
Yes, Mom.

241
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:01,680
So will you finish everything in time?

242
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:05,880
I'm not sure.

243
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:09,240
Well, what if you don't?

244
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:11,400
You'll embarrass me.

245
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:15,360
I'm really sorry, Mom.

246
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,040
I'll try my best.

247
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:19,840
You'd better hurry up, then.

248
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:21,960
I don't want it to turn out bad.

249
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:24,200
Sure, Mom.

250
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:50,280
You can come out now.

251
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:58,160
Girls, I'm sorry
on behalf of my daughter-in-law.

252
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:01,080
She couldn't get everything ready in time.

253
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:04,560
It's just how rich kids are.

254
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,720
Normally,

255
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:08,000
her maid does everything for her,

256
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:10,880
so when I leave her in charge,
she can't do it.

257
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,960
Please don't get mad at her.

258
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:27,920
You brat.

259
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,840
This time, I'll win.

260
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,480
The appetizer's good, isn't it?

261
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,720
- Oh, yes, it is!
- Wait until you try the entrée.

262
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,120
It's so good.

263
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:44,160
- Really?
- Of course!

264
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:45,760
I can't wait.

265
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:47,440
I hope you all like it.

266
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:49,240
The presentation's so mouth-watering.

267
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:51,320
- True.
- Thank you so much.

268
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:52,880
Can't wait to eat it.

269
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:55,080
The food's so good, isn't it?

270
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,280
Yeah. All the dishes look so good.

271
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:01,120
Oh, Ging!

272
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:02,360
Come join us!

273
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:04,520
Mom.

274
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:06,480
- Come on.
- Come sit with us.

275
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:09,000
- It looks so good, doesn't it?
- Yeah.

276
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:10,280
Oh, I can't wait.

277
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:14,720
You know, Ging,
I've got to hand it to them.

278
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:16,800
Neen and Runch are so sweet.

279
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:18,520
They really took great care of us.

280
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:20,200
Yeah.

281
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:21,680
She's so polite and caring.

282
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:24,200
And everything looks well-prepared.

283
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:25,760
Mom,

284
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:28,360
Neen's prepared
a fine dining meal for you.

285
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:30,880
It's from a famous restaurant in Bangkok.

286
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:34,600
Luckily, my parents love this restaurant,

287
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:37,160
so they sent their chefs over just for us.

288
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:39,800
Normally, they don't do off-site catering.

289
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:41,680
- Wow!
- Wow!

290
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:43,680
Your daughter-in-law sure has connections.

291
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:45,760
Oh, come on.

292
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:47,520
She's really something.

293
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:49,600
She's both talented and sophisticated.

294
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:50,960
That's right.

295
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:54,720
Ging, can you host a party
like this again someday?

296
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:57,520
We'll come, no matter how far away we are.

297
00:23:57,600 --> 00:23:59,640
That's right! I loved it.

298
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:03,160
I was really impressed today.

299
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:05,640
Let's do this again.
I'm so happy to have you over.

300
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:07,680
I'll invite you again someday.

301
00:24:07,760 --> 00:24:09,720
- Sure.
- Sounds good.

302
00:24:09,800 --> 00:24:12,280
See, we're both full and happy.

303
00:24:13,280 --> 00:24:16,200
- Thank you for coming.
- Aw.

304
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:18,400
- Let's meet again soon.
- Sure.

305
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:20,280
- We'll get going now.
- Okay.

306
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:21,200
Drive safe.

307
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:22,720
- Okay.
- If you'll excuse me.

308
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:23,760
- Sure.
- We'll come again.

309
00:24:23,840 --> 00:24:25,200
- See you, Ging.
- Take care.

310
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:26,440
Bye.

311
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:30,280
Good job, Neen.

312
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:32,520
I'm proud of you.

313
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:34,520
So where's my reward?

314
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:36,720
I'll give you one tonight.

315
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:38,440
Hey, can't you see

316
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:40,800
your mother's standing here?

317
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:48,240
Anyway, I need to use the bathroom.

318
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:03,440
You did it to embarrass me, didn't you?

319
00:25:05,280 --> 00:25:07,600
That was never my idea, Mom.

320
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:09,680
I just want what's best for you--

321
00:25:09,760 --> 00:25:11,920
Drop the act already.

322
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:18,200
I really doubt
someone like you could change.

323
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:23,120
Why are you laughing?

324
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:27,880
Couldn't keep up the act,
so you finally snapped?

325
00:25:27,960 --> 00:25:30,160
This was your plan, wasn't it?

326
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:32,560
What are you talking about?

327
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:34,080
I'm an innocent girl.

328
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:36,000
I'd never scheme against you.

329
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:37,200
You're so full of it!

330
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:39,840
You're just a rude little brat.

331
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:41,800
You think you're smart?

332
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,360
Don't think I can't see through you.

333
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:49,400
I'll make Runch hate you so much

334
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:51,760
that she'll never want
to see your face again.

335
00:25:57,600 --> 00:25:59,880
- Help me, Runch! Help!
- You're crazy!

336
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,720
No! Runch!

337
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:05,320
- Runch! Runch!
- Crazy bitch! Let go!

338
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:06,920
- Help me, Runch!
- You're crazy!

339
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,600
Help me! Help!

340
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:12,800
Runch! Runch! Runch!

341
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:14,400
- Runch, help!
- Enough.

342
00:26:14,480 --> 00:26:15,880
Stop it!

343
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:17,320
- Stop it!
- Runch!

344
00:26:19,600 --> 00:26:20,440
Runch,

345
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:23,280
Neen hurt me, Runch.

346
00:26:24,040 --> 00:26:25,280
Crazy bitch!

347
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:26,480
That's enough, Mom.

348
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:31,760
I'm calling Dad so he can take you home.

349
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:33,520
Why?

350
00:26:35,040 --> 00:26:36,160
Watch this.

351
00:26:38,720 --> 00:26:41,680
<i>I'll make Runch hate you so much</i>

352
00:26:41,760 --> 00:26:44,120
<i>that she'll never want</i>
<i>to see your face again.</i>

353
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:51,440
<i>Help me, Runch!</i>

354
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:54,280
- You installed a security camera…
<i>- You're crazy!</i>

355
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:56,160
- …to spy on me?
<i>- Help me! Help!</i>

356
00:26:56,960 --> 00:26:58,200
Yes.

357
00:26:58,280 --> 00:27:00,240
I did it the day you threw away my ring.

358
00:27:08,320 --> 00:27:09,880
Please let me explain, Runch.

359
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:11,040
- No.
- Please?

360
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:14,120
I saw everything.

361
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:16,080
I saw what you did.

362
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:20,040
I can't let you stay here anymore.

363
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:28,720
You planned this, didn't you, Peeracha?

364
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:30,520
Didn't you, Peeracha?

365
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:32,200
That's enough. Mom!

366
00:27:32,280 --> 00:27:33,360
Stop it!

367
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:37,320
Don't you lay a finger on Neen.

368
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,880
Don't hurt her.

369
00:27:40,080 --> 00:27:42,480
I did it all by myself.

370
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:49,200
Runch…

371
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:53,880
You should pack your things.

372
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:57,720
I'm calling Dad so he can take you home.

373
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:04,440
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

374
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:39,080
Your mom's gone home already?

375
00:28:54,240 --> 00:28:56,760
I know it must be difficult for you.

376
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:02,160
If you want to talk or vent,

377
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:04,400
I'm always here to listen.

378
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:24,160
Getting to hug you

379
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:27,680
and having some peace and quiet

380
00:29:29,120 --> 00:29:30,760
is enough to cheer me up.

381
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:35,880
Then I'll hug you tighter.

382
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:58,040
I think we've been
too stressed out lately.

383
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:02,080
Can you take me on a trip?

384
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:11,320
I want to be with you like this all day
and just do nothing.

385
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:16,280
Won't you get bored if we do this all day?

386
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:18,400
Of course I won't.

387
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:21,280
Just seeing your face makes me happy.

388
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:23,560
Me too.

389
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:00,320
What are you doing?

390
00:31:01,840 --> 00:31:02,840
I'm building a house.

391
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:05,480
A house just for the two of us.

392
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:22,400
It's all gone!

393
00:31:25,800 --> 00:31:27,880
That's alright.

394
00:31:27,960 --> 00:31:29,240
We can build a new one.

395
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:32,400
This time, I'll help you build it.

396
00:31:36,600 --> 00:31:37,720
Fine.

397
00:31:40,680 --> 00:31:41,720
Come on.

398
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:09,880
Hello.

399
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:15,960
Yes, I'm Gingkamol, Runchlaphat's mother.

400
00:32:19,560 --> 00:32:20,680
A show?

401
00:32:20,760 --> 00:32:22,040
A show, you say?

402
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:31,520
You're almost there.

403
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:33,640
Just a little longer.

404
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:37,680
In five, four, three, one.

405
00:32:37,760 --> 00:32:38,800
Here we are.

406
00:32:39,640 --> 00:32:40,640
Are you ready?

407
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:41,640
Yes.

408
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:52,400
‪Ta-da!

409
00:32:53,760 --> 00:32:55,360
And this is

410
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:58,200
where we're staying tonight.

411
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:00,280
- Yay!
- Yay!

412
00:33:00,360 --> 00:33:02,480
You're the sweetest!

413
00:33:02,560 --> 00:33:04,000
- You like it?
- Thank you.

414
00:33:04,080 --> 00:33:06,240
- Do you like it?
- I love it.

415
00:33:07,520 --> 00:33:08,520
Wow.

416
00:33:21,800 --> 00:33:22,880
Are you hungry?

417
00:33:23,600 --> 00:33:24,960
Hold tight a little longer.

418
00:33:25,040 --> 00:33:26,280
It's almost ready.

419
00:33:28,360 --> 00:33:30,480
Can I help you with anything?

420
00:33:31,840 --> 00:33:32,960
No.

421
00:33:33,040 --> 00:33:34,800
Just sit tight.

422
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:36,320
Because today,

423
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:38,040
you're my princess.

424
00:33:39,120 --> 00:33:40,080
Yes, ma'am.

425
00:33:40,760 --> 00:33:41,640
Yes.

426
00:33:44,680 --> 00:33:47,400
Hey. Stop. Stop it.

427
00:33:48,280 --> 00:33:49,800
I told you,

428
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:51,840
you're my princess today.

429
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:54,520
Don't do anything by yourself.
I'll do it for you.

430
00:33:55,440 --> 00:33:56,520
Okay.

431
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:00,120
Here it comes.

432
00:34:13,239 --> 00:34:15,000
The shrimp is so sweet.

433
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:18,880
I bet it's because you grilled it for me.

434
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:21,560
- Want some more?
- Yeah.

435
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:31,719
Can you pour me another?

436
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:41,080
Neen.

437
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:43,360
The bottle's empty.

438
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:45,920
Empty. Gone.

439
00:34:48,199 --> 00:34:51,080
But I want another.

440
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:53,480
You should stop.

441
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:58,560
We're out. No, no, no. You're drunk.

442
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:04,320
Will you still love me if I'm drunk?

443
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:05,680
I will.

444
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:08,400
Drunk or not, I'll love you either way.

445
00:35:09,920 --> 00:35:11,080
I'm so glad.

446
00:35:14,520 --> 00:35:15,840
- Huh?
- Then let's go.

447
00:35:16,720 --> 00:35:18,640
Wait-- Where are you going, Neen?

448
00:35:20,320 --> 00:35:22,200
Let's dance.

449
00:35:22,920 --> 00:35:24,600
But there's no music.

450
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:26,280
We don't need a song.

451
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:28,560
We'll dance to the song in here.

452
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:30,640
My song?

453
00:35:30,720 --> 00:35:31,800
In here.

454
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,320
Your song too?

455
00:35:42,200 --> 00:35:44,320
And then you grab my waist.

456
00:35:44,920 --> 00:35:47,600
Like so. Right.

457
00:35:47,680 --> 00:35:48,920
And right.

458
00:35:57,520 --> 00:35:58,800
We should stop.

459
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:01,760
You're drunk, Neen.

460
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:04,280
And if you don't stop,

461
00:36:05,840 --> 00:36:08,200
I won't be able to stop myself.

462
00:36:10,560 --> 00:36:12,400
Then don't.

463
00:36:27,600 --> 00:36:28,800
No.

464
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:31,200
Remember,

465
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:34,440
you're my princess tonight.

466
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:38,680
I'll do everything for you.

467
00:37:05,400 --> 00:37:06,880
Thank you so much

468
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:08,920
for taking the time
to be on our show today.

469
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:10,680
It's my pleasure.

470
00:37:10,760 --> 00:37:12,720
As long as it benefits society.

471
00:37:12,800 --> 00:37:15,320
Actually, our show, <i>Real Talk With Moms</i>

472
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:17,120
is meant to be a space

473
00:37:17,200 --> 00:37:19,200
where parents can voice
their true feelings,

474
00:37:19,800 --> 00:37:22,120
especially about sexual diversity.

475
00:37:22,200 --> 00:37:23,720
We want the public to see

476
00:37:23,800 --> 00:37:26,760
that not every family
can easily accept it.

477
00:37:26,840 --> 00:37:28,680
But trying to understand it

478
00:37:28,760 --> 00:37:30,840
is already an important first step.

479
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:32,920
I think so too.

480
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:35,680
Matters like this aren't easy for mothers.

481
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:38,320
That's right. We wanted to invite you

482
00:37:38,400 --> 00:37:40,800
because you're
one of the mothers who accepted

483
00:37:40,880 --> 00:37:42,560
your daughter's same-sex marriage,

484
00:37:42,640 --> 00:37:45,040
which not everyone can do.

485
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:49,640
I may not understand it all,

486
00:37:49,720 --> 00:37:52,520
but I love my daughter.
And that should be enough.

487
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:55,200
That's exactly the idea
we're trying to convey.

488
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:56,440
The questions we ask

489
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:58,240
aren't intended to attack anyone.

490
00:37:58,320 --> 00:38:01,280
We just want to tell each story
through a mother's lens.

491
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:04,480
What she had to go through
before she could accept the truth.

492
00:38:04,560 --> 00:38:06,760
There's nothing to worry about.

493
00:38:06,840 --> 00:38:08,480
Just say whatever you feel.

494
00:38:08,560 --> 00:38:09,960
Say it from your heart.

495
00:38:10,040 --> 00:38:11,400
We believe the viewers

496
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:13,920
will see that you only want
what's best for your daughter.

497
00:38:14,800 --> 00:38:17,400
Then, I'll say how I really feel.

498
00:38:17,480 --> 00:38:19,240
- Sure.
- So everyone

499
00:38:19,320 --> 00:38:21,000
will understand a mother's love.

500
00:38:21,600 --> 00:38:22,600
Yes.

501
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:27,040
Ma'am, we'll start in five minutes.

502
00:38:27,120 --> 00:38:28,120
Okay.

503
00:38:37,160 --> 00:38:40,600
Lately, people have been talking
about your dear daughter's relationship.

504
00:38:40,680 --> 00:38:42,120
How do you feel about this?

505
00:38:42,920 --> 00:38:44,720
I, um…

506
00:38:45,320 --> 00:38:46,720
I do admit

507
00:38:46,800 --> 00:38:48,920
that it's not something I expected.

508
00:38:49,480 --> 00:38:50,840
But in the end,

509
00:38:50,920 --> 00:38:53,600
no matter what path you choose in life,

510
00:38:53,680 --> 00:38:55,880
I'll always love you just the same, honey.

511
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:57,120
I'm just…

512
00:38:57,800 --> 00:38:58,880
worried about you.

513
00:38:58,960 --> 00:39:00,600
Many people see

514
00:39:00,680 --> 00:39:02,160
your daughter's love

515
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:04,360
as the courage to be herself.

516
00:39:04,440 --> 00:39:05,960
Do you agree?

517
00:39:06,040 --> 00:39:08,680
I don't believe it's wrong to be yourself.

518
00:39:09,560 --> 00:39:10,880
But sometimes,

519
00:39:10,960 --> 00:39:12,840
the people in your life

520
00:39:12,920 --> 00:39:15,240
may fail to consider all the consequences,

521
00:39:15,320 --> 00:39:16,840
especially for your family.

522
00:39:16,920 --> 00:39:20,120
So you don't approve
of her current relationship?

523
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:22,640
I don't want to say I don't approve it.

524
00:39:24,040 --> 00:39:26,320
I just want you to have an easy life,

525
00:39:26,960 --> 00:39:30,400
where you don't have to go
against the public opinion,

526
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:33,960
where you don't have
to sacrifice anything for anyone's love.

527
00:39:34,560 --> 00:39:36,040
Rumor has it

528
00:39:36,120 --> 00:39:39,120
that you and Ms. Peeracha
fight quite often.

529
00:39:39,200 --> 00:39:40,280
Is that true?

530
00:39:40,840 --> 00:39:42,880
I've never had a fight with anyone.

531
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:45,840
I'm just straightforward.

532
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:47,840
And I just

533
00:39:47,920 --> 00:39:50,880
want to protect my daughter, is all.

534
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:52,960
If one day,

535
00:39:53,040 --> 00:39:54,920
your daughter has to choose between

536
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:56,520
family and love,

537
00:39:56,600 --> 00:39:58,280
what do you want her to choose?

538
00:40:11,240 --> 00:40:13,240
I don't want her to have to choose.

539
00:40:20,120 --> 00:40:21,640
But if love

540
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:25,480
makes you turn against your family,

541
00:40:27,760 --> 00:40:29,680
I have no choice but to leave you alone…

542
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:33,640
and hope that one day

543
00:40:36,200 --> 00:40:38,200
you'll understand how a mother feels.

544
00:40:43,120 --> 00:40:45,800
If Ms. Peeracha watches this show,

545
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:47,800
do you have something to tell her?

546
00:40:55,040 --> 00:40:56,400
I was never angry

547
00:40:57,160 --> 00:40:58,720
or hateful toward anyone.

548
00:41:00,400 --> 00:41:02,280
I just want her to know that

549
00:41:03,640 --> 00:41:05,280
loving someone

550
00:41:06,840 --> 00:41:09,360
shouldn't come at the cost of breaking…

551
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:12,960
a mother's heart.

552
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:34,560
1 YEAR AGO

553
00:41:34,640 --> 00:41:36,640
Over the two years we've been together,

554
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:39,040
we've been through a lot, haven't we?

555
00:41:41,240 --> 00:41:43,000
Just seeing your face

556
00:41:43,680 --> 00:41:46,720
makes me feel like
everything will get easier.

557
00:41:56,920 --> 00:41:58,680
If we ever feel tired,

558
00:42:00,400 --> 00:42:02,440
can I stay by your side just like this?

559
00:42:04,320 --> 00:42:05,480
Of course.

560
00:42:06,240 --> 00:42:07,200
No matter when,

561
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:09,920
my arms will always be open for you.

562
00:42:10,880 --> 00:42:13,440
Then, do you promise

563
00:42:14,080 --> 00:42:16,360
that we'll always be each other's home?

564
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:19,320
I promise.

565
00:42:20,080 --> 00:42:21,720
I won't let go now.

566
00:42:29,520 --> 00:42:30,600
Are you ready?

567
00:42:31,400 --> 00:42:32,640
- Yes.
- Yes.

568
00:42:41,240 --> 00:42:42,520
Are you ready, Ms. Peeracha?

569
00:42:42,600 --> 00:42:44,600
- Yes.
- Okay.

570
00:42:45,200 --> 00:42:48,120
What do you like about Ms. Runchlaphat?

571
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:54,080
I'll keep it short.

572
00:42:55,880 --> 00:42:58,240
Runch is someone who makes me feel

573
00:42:59,400 --> 00:43:01,440
like I don't have to try to be anyone.

574
00:43:02,920 --> 00:43:04,840
Normally, I'm the type

575
00:43:04,920 --> 00:43:07,040
to overthink and imagine things,

576
00:43:07,120 --> 00:43:09,120
wondering if I'm good enough.

577
00:43:10,160 --> 00:43:12,800
But when I'm with her,

578
00:43:13,680 --> 00:43:15,200
she makes me feel like

579
00:43:15,800 --> 00:43:18,280
I don't have to be capable or strong,

580
00:43:18,360 --> 00:43:20,920
and I don't have to feel okay
all the time.

581
00:43:22,120 --> 00:43:25,720
As long as I'm me,
she'll always be by my side.

582
00:43:27,120 --> 00:43:28,960
Plus,

583
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:31,120
Runch is the type of person who,

584
00:43:31,200 --> 00:43:33,520
even if the whole world was against me,

585
00:43:33,600 --> 00:43:36,160
would always be there for me

586
00:43:36,240 --> 00:43:38,560
without asking questions.

587
00:43:40,080 --> 00:43:42,720
It just feels so secure

588
00:43:42,800 --> 00:43:45,240
to have someone
who you can take a rest with,

589
00:43:45,320 --> 00:43:46,880
cry with,

590
00:43:46,960 --> 00:43:49,480
and dream of a future with.

591
00:43:51,760 --> 00:43:52,720
There.

592
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:55,680
If you asked me what I like about her,
that would be my answer.

593
00:43:58,360 --> 00:43:59,320
Wait.

594
00:44:00,240 --> 00:44:02,120
That was so long.
That wasn't short at all.

595
00:44:02,800 --> 00:44:03,920
Was it too long?

596
00:44:07,040 --> 00:44:09,080
If it were me,
of course I'd choose my mother.

597
00:44:09,160 --> 00:44:12,720
Your words
made the whole country see it that way.

598
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:15,400
- See what?
- That Neen's the one who took me

599
00:44:15,480 --> 00:44:16,600
away from you.

600
00:44:16,680 --> 00:44:19,320
If you choose to keep this up,

601
00:44:19,400 --> 00:44:21,120
I'll have to decide.

602
00:44:22,240 --> 00:44:23,880
Runch, Runch!

603
00:44:23,960 --> 00:44:25,880
From now on, no matter what we face,

604
00:44:25,960 --> 00:44:27,680
we won't let go of each other's hands.

605
00:44:27,760 --> 00:44:29,680
I feel so lucky

606
00:44:30,280 --> 00:44:31,840
to have you by my side.

607
00:45:18,400 --> 00:45:20,400
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya
